    <fr:route>/def-005A/</fr:route>
    <fr:title text="Left and Right Inverses">Left and Right Inverses</fr:title>
    <fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>
    Let <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[f:A\to  B]]></fr:tex>. A <html:strong>left inverse</html:strong> of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[f]]></fr:tex> is precisely a
    <fr:link href="/def-005H/" title="Retraction of a Map" uri="https://caimeo.space/def-005H/" display-uri="def-005H" type="local">retraction of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[f]]></fr:tex></fr:link>, while a <html:strong>right inverse</html:strong> of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[f]]></fr:tex> is
    precisely a <fr:link href="/def-005G/" title="Section of a Map" uri="https://caimeo.space/def-005G/" display-uri="def-005G" type="local">section of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[f]]></fr:tex></fr:link>. Thus
    <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
        \mathsf {hasLeftInverse}(f)
        :\equiv \mathsf {retr}(f),\qquad 
        \mathsf {hasRightInverse}(f)
        :\equiv \mathsf {sec}(f).
    ]]></fr:tex></html:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
