        <fr:title text="Backlinks">Backlinks</fr:title>
      </fr:frontmatter>
      <fr:mainmatter>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://caimeo.space/def-005B/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>def-005B</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/def-005B/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="Bi-invertible Map">Bi-invertible Map</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>
    A map <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[f:A\to  B]]></fr:tex> is <html:strong>bi-invertible</html:strong> if it has both a
    <fr:link href="/def-005G/" title="Section of a Map" uri="https://caimeo.space/def-005G/" display-uri="def-005G" type="local">section</fr:link> and a <fr:link href="/def-005H/" title="Retraction of a Map" uri="https://caimeo.space/def-005H/" display-uri="def-005H" type="local">retraction</fr:link>, or equivalently a separate
    <fr:link href="/def-005A/" title="Left and Right Inverses" uri="https://caimeo.space/def-005A/" display-uri="def-005A" type="local">right and left inverse</fr:link>. Define
    <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
        \mathsf {isBiInv}(f)
        :\equiv 
        \mathsf {sec}(f)\times \mathsf {retr}(f).
    ]]></fr:tex>
    The left and right inverse maps are supplied independently; their inverse
    laws imply that they are homotopic.
</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
      </fr:mainmatter>
    </fr:tree>
    <fr:tree show-metadata="false" hidden-when-empty="true">
      <fr:frontmatter>
